#
# CT2 counter-example (Don't), family axis: two gmeow:EmbeddingFamily nodes that
# differ in gmeow:executionContract (fp32/deterministic vs fp16/non-deterministic — a
# material generation-contract component that changes the produced vector VALUES) yet
# carry the SAME gmeow:contentDigest. Two materially different generation contracts
# must never share one family identity. Triggers distinct-family-id.rq (→ the pair
# ce:famCollideA, ce:famCollideB). Exercises the execution/subject-projection/
# generation-normalization axes gmeow:VectorSpaceContract does not carry, so competency
# test 2 covers the family generation contract, not only the effective space.
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ce:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/counter-examples/embedding-projection/> .

ce:famCollideA a gmeow:EmbeddingFamily ;
    gmeow:executionContract "fp32;deterministic=true" ;
    gmeow:contentDigest     "blake3:fada000011112222333344445555666677778888999900001111222233334444" .

ce:famCollideB a gmeow:EmbeddingFamily ;
    gmeow:executionContract "fp16;deterministic=false" ;
    gmeow:contentDigest     "blake3:fada000011112222333344445555666677778888999900001111222233334444" .
